WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
Deliver even without a signal.
Historical iOS simulator build · Controlled Demo

00:05.000 --> 00:14.000
Switch Offline and keep working.
Results will be saved on this device.

00:14.000 --> 00:21.000
Complete the first stop.
The result and its queued event commit together.

00:21.000 --> 00:27.000
Record a failed delivery with a reason.
Both terminal outcomes are saved locally.

00:27.000 --> 00:43.000
Two results saved; two confirmations still pending.
Saved does not mean confirmed.

00:43.000 --> 00:49.000
Terminate the actual OS process.
Keep the same installation and database.

00:49.000 --> 00:54.000
A new process reopens the database.
Both results and the two queued updates survive.

00:54.000 --> 00:59.000
Return Online. Send the queue serially.
Confirmations come from a controlled HTTP fixture.

00:59.000 --> 01:06.000
Both matching confirmations are now durable.
Only then does the queue reach zero.

01:06.000 --> 01:11.000
Restart once more.
Confirmed operations are not resent.

01:11.000 --> 01:22.000
Three real processes: 21377 → 21604 → 21697.
Reliable local saving; traceable simulated confirmation.
